+# 2026-04-26
+
+## `/full-review` iteration 1 + batch-1 fixes (12+ findings, V4-1 → V4-19, V4-21)
+
+**Action:** First full-codebase multi-AI review of the day, after the 42-commit `createSimulationBridge.ts` shrink session merged to main earlier.
+
+**Reviewers:**
+- Codex (`gpt-5.4` @ `model_reasoning_effort=xhigh`, `--sandbox read-only --ephemeral`).
+- Gemini (`gemini-3.1-pro-preview` @ `--approval-mode plan`). Without `--approval-mode plan`, gemini-3.x tries to call `run_shell_command` / `invoke_agent` and produces zero output.
+- Claude (`opus` @ `--effort xhigh`, `claude -p "<prompt>" --allowedTools "..."`).
+
+Findings synthesized to `docs/reviews/full/2026-04-26/1/REVIEW.md`. The 42-commit shrink itself was structurally safe — all three reviewers verified side-map ownership is centralized (in `bridgeState.ts` now, no longer `createWorld`), system-registration order is determinism-safe (driven by explicit `before`/`after` deps), and the `wirePostSeedOps` revert + restore (`9818df8` → `c73649b` → `4cbc1bf`) was byte-identical to the original extraction.
+
+The strongest cross-reviewer agreement was a **type-safety hole in the wiring seam**: 10 unsafe `as RegisterAllSystemsArg` casts in `registerBridgeSystems.ts` were typing each ops factory result as bare `object` and asserting the spread covered the full target shape. Claude proved the hole was real: `RegisterAllSystemsDeps` declared `beginTrebuchetUnpack` / `beginTrebuchetPack` as `=> boolean`, but the actual `TrebuchetStateOps` implementations return `void`. The cast hid the drift.
+
+The next strongest agreement was **doc drift** — all three reviewers caught that `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `drift-log.md`, `devlog/summary.md` reflected a pre-Phase-5 world (claimed `2722` lines, actual was `332`; named ~30 modules out of ~45; said "side-map ownership lives in createWorld" though it now lives in `bridgeState.ts`). Plus the detailed devlog filename `2026-04-24_2026-04-25.md` was date-invalid (contained 2026-04-26 entries).
+
+**Code reviewer comments by AI provider, by theme:**
+- **Codex:** type-safety hole at registerBridgeSystems (V4-1); fog-memory delete path uses anchor-only visibility on multi-cell buildings (V4-2 — sibling of iter-3 V3-1 on the cleanup side); save-load wastes scenario gen (V4-3); doc drift across ARCHITECTURE.md, drift-log, devlog summary, devlog filename (V4-4).
+- **Gemini:** quadratic loops in efficiency hot spots — `assignNearestResource` allocates wrappers for every resource pre-filter (V4-1); `getHumanUnitIdsInRect` / `getHumanOwnedSheepIdsInRect` allocate wrappers for every unit/sheep pre-bbox (V4-2); drift-log stale (V4-3); aiSystem.ts at ~492 LOC (V4-4); `transformOps.syncSpawnedEntityOccupancy` swallows all errors (V4-5).
+- **Claude:** type-safety hole + existence proof of trebuchet signature drift (V4-1, V4-3); architecture/drift-log/devlog summary stale across the board (V4-2, V4-4, V4-5); humanInputOps switch fall-through (V4-6); 4 `void` markers exposing dead dep-bag fields (V4-7); `gathererDropOffStuckSinceTick` not in save blob (V4-8); monk convert per-tick guard timing (V4-9); `playerHasConquestPresence` quadratic in player count (V4-10); `assignAiMonkTasks` waste when AI has no monks (V4-11); fog-memory comment stale on resource path (V4-12); dead type re-exports (V4-13); unnecessary `Map.entries()` spread (V4-14); types still imported from facade (V4-15); versioning + changelog drift (V4-16); EOF formatting (V4-18).
+
+**Result:** Iter-1 batch-1 commits on `agent/review-findings-2026-04-26-iter1-batch1`:
+- `608048f` **[V4-1, V4-2]** Drop type-erasing casts in `registerBridgeSystems` wiring; type each ops factory's spread to its actual return interface (`PlayerQueries` / `AiDecisionOps` / `TargetFindingOps` / `TrebuchetStateOps` / `MovementPlanOps` / `EntityDestroyOps` / `EntityCreateOps` / `MonkTaskOps` / `TransformOps` / `MatchEndOps`) and fix the resulting type drift on `beginTrebuchetUnpack` / `beginTrebuchetPack` (boolean → void).
+- `0307397` **[V4-3]** Footprint-aware fog-memory delete path. New fixture `fog-memory-castle-destroy-edge-fixture` (low-HP castle + Siege Ram with vision radius 1 + scout that sees only a non-anchor cell); regression test verified to fail pre-fix and pass post-fix.
+- `15faac2` **[V4-7]** `gathererDropOffStuckSinceTick` round-trips through `SaveBlob` (saveSchema field + saveGameOps write + hydrateFromSavedGame read + V3-8 orphan-key prune extension).
+- `2309942` **[V4-13, V4-15, V4-16, V4-17, V4-18]** Cleanliness sweep: humanInputOps explicit `default: return false`; transformOps catch logs unexpected occupancy errors; drop `enqueueRejection` from WirePostSeedDeps + `isAiMilitaryUnit` from RegisterAllSystemsDeps (the `void` markers existed only to suppress lint); drop unnecessary `Map.entries()` snapshot spread; delete dead `BuildingComponent` / `UnitComponent` re-exports.
+- `fbfcf40` **[V4-19]** Extract `bridge/sharedTypes.ts` for `UnitCommand` / `MonkTask` / `ConstructionState` / `TrebuchetPackState`. Six bridge children + `bridgeState` no longer reach back to the facade for shared types. Facade re-exports them so external consumers keep stable import paths.
+- `380e741` **[V4-14]** Tick-tag the per-target Monk convert guard. Replace `Set<number>` with `Map<number, number>` keyed by target id, valued by tick. The consumer checks `=== activeWorld.tick` so the per-tick contract holds even if the periodic `.clear()` misses a phase boundary.
+- `0c32253` **[V4-8, V4-9, V4-10, V4-12]** Efficiency batch: lazy scenario gen on save-load; inline-filter optimization for `assignNearestResource` and `getHumanUnitIdsInRect` / `getHumanOwnedSheepIdsInRect` (no per-entity wrapper allocations pre-filter); `assignAiMonkTasks` skip when AI owns no Monks.
+
+Plus the doc + AGENTS.md refresh in this commit (V4-4 / V4-5 / V4-6 / V4-21 / V4-23 / V4-25):
+- `ARCHITECTURE.md` `bridge/` paragraph rewritten to enumerate the orchestration / state / systems / ops / types tiers with the actual ~45 modules; "side-map ownership lives in createWorld" sentence updated to reference `bridgeState.ts`; Phaser scene paragraph adds `buildingRenderer.ts`.
+- `drift-log.md` adds Phase-5 follow-up rows for the `createWorld` move + `bridgeState` extract + `wireBridgeOps` / `wirePostSeedOps` / `assembleBridgeApi` / `registerBridgeSystems` / `registerAllSystems` / `scenarioSeedOps` / `hydrateFromSavedGame` / `monkAiSearchHelpers` / `monkTaskAppliers` / `selectionFinders` / `renderStateOps` / `sharedTypes` extractions plus the Phase-4 phase row's actual final size (332 LOC, -96%).
+- `devlog/summary.md` head entry updated to reflect the 7606 → 332 final size.
+- `2026-04-24_2026-04-25.md` renamed to `2026-04-24_2026-04-26.md` (date range now covers the 2026-04-26 entries already appended) per the AGENTS.md devlog convention; new file `2026-04-26_2026-04-26.md` started for this iter-4 review entry.
+- `AGENTS.md` Code-review CLI examples refreshed: Gemini line gains `--approval-mode plan` (without it, gemini-3.x tries to call `run_shell_command` / `invoke_agent` and produces zero output); Codex note added that PowerShell `Select-String` invocations get blocked by `--sandbox read-only` on Windows (the model recovers via direct file reads).
+- `fogMemorySystem.ts` resource-loop comment updated to note that anchor-only visibility is correct because every memorable resource is 1×1 (V4-21 defensive guard for future multi-cell resources).
+
